.TH TRAIT 1 "2026-10-01" "trait 0.2" "General Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
trait \- author, teach, and evaluate Bench workers and teams
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B trait
.BR create " | " edit " | " train " | " eval
.RI [ \-request " TEXT"]
.RI [ \-m " MODEL"]
.RI [ \-turns " N"]
.RI [ \-timeout " D"]
.RI [ \-entry-boundary " host|cage"]
.I INPUT_DIR NEW_OUTPUT_DIR
.br
.B trait
.BR help " | " version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Trait uses Hire's existing creator to assemble the instructions, checks,
programs, and specialists needed for an outcome. It prepares missing evaluation
material, reviews the exact selection, and runs fresh cases automatically.
Workers and Brief skills retain their existing formats.
.PP
Flags follow the action and precede both directories. Input is untouched;
output must be new and disjoint from input and private controller storage.
There is no interactive prompt, stdin request, implicit resume, in-place edit,
automatic retry, or library publication.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B create
Author a new capability from REQUEST.md or -request and selected sources.
Structurally verify, prepare evaluation, review, and run fresh cases.
.TP
.B edit
Revise expert/ for the selected request, including code and team wiring when
needed. Continue through automatic evaluation.
.TP
.B train
Teach expert/ from supplied knowledge or a checked recovery. Freeze at least
one transfer and one regression case before the amendment; generate missing
cases first. Without train.json, use knowledge/private. Explicit settings
must specify valid kind and scope.
.PP
Training changes only nonexecutable Markdown. Preserve all other paths, modes,
and bytes, including all executables and executable Markdown. Refuse new
executable Markdown. Use edit for code, data, checker, or runtime changes.
Only accepted fresh cases justify retained_on_cases. This neither trains
model weights nor proves improvement over the original or causal skill use.
.TP
.B eval
Evaluate expert/ without amending it. Use selected cases or generate them
from the documented capability. Emit no replacement expert.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-request " TEXT"
Override REQUEST.md in the admitted input without changing the input directory.
.TP
.BI \-m " MODEL"
Select a configured model; otherwise use ASK_MODEL or the provider default.
.TP
.BI \-turns " N"
Worker turn limit; default 12.
.TP
.BI \-timeout " D"
Timeout per subprocess; default 5m. Includes each authoring, review, complete
controller entry, worker, and check invocation. Not a monetary budget or total
case-suite deadline.
.TP
.BI \-entry-boundary " host|cage"
Controller execution boundary. Default host preserves existing team and child
Agent compatibility with ordinary host authority. Cage requests an additional
write boundary; unavailable or unsupported nested confinement fails with 125,
without fallback to host. Ordinary worker execution remains through Agent.
.SH INPUT
Create needs REQUEST.md or -request. Edit and train also need expert/.
Eval needs expert/. Optional sources/ contains selected supporting material.
Optional cases/ or evaluation/cases/ provides caller criteria; do not supply
both. Optional evaluation/run.json selects an entry. CAPABILITIES.md records
an existing capability assessment. Original worker.lock.json and team.lock.json
remain starting-source provenance; edited bytes do not inherit unchanged locks.
.PP
An authored Trait output can be selected directly for edit/train with a new
-request, or for fresh eval. Reuse its expert and evaluation recipe; exclude
its old cases/ work results from current case inputs.
Training from a prior result preserves its cases and adds a new transfer case
for the teaching request before amending the definition.
.PP
A separate Hire evaluation preparation supplies missing cases or assessment.
Its copied expert and supplied evaluation files must remain unchanged.
CAPABILITIES.md covers instructions, checks, programs/apps, specialists,
dependencies, entry, and handoffs, including unnecessary categories.
.PP
For explicit knowledge training, train.json selects kind knowledge and scope
general or private. General scope excludes private organizational facts.
Private scope grants no filesystem confidentiality or publication authority.
Recovery additionally names an absolute original session and destination skill.
Hone checks eligibility, prepares an exact proposal, and admits it only after
bounded Ask model review approves those bytes. No useful lesson is a no-change
outcome; no other route is substituted.
.SH REVIEW
Before execution, Ask reviews the exact definition, capability assessment,
entry, and frozen cases. Require approval and a reason. REVIEW.md records
automated model review, not human approval or proof of safety or quality.
A negative, invalid, or stale decision stops evaluation.
.SH CASES
Each cases/ID has goal.md, optional input/, executable check, case.json, and
optional expected data. case.json selects purpose transfer, regression, or
general and outputs, an array of relative artifact paths.
Generated suites and training require both transfer and regression cases.
Generated labels are model-authored judgments, not independent domain truth.
.PP
After execution, Trait snapshots work in separate storage, outside write grants
when controller Cage is selected. Host controllers can still alter snapshots.
The independent check runs with no argv from this snapshot. TRAIT_CASE_DIR
names the frozen case. Record binds every case file and declared output.
Check Cage denies networking and workspace writes while allowing private
temporary files. Exit 0 accepts, 1 rejects, and another status means broken.
Publish the captured bytes, not a later reread of mutable execution work.
Separate storage does not isolate authority from a host controller.
.PP
The expert's own verifier retains Agent/Ply's existing contract; ordinary
Agent checks run outside its action Cage. The independent case check is
separate. Host reads remain available, so expectations are visible regression
material, not hidden tests. Acceptance establishes only what the checks cover.
.SH ENTRIES
Without evaluation/run.json, use Agent with fresh work and -B.
A controller recipe supplies entry, args, and optional requires. The entry is
a regular executable relative to expert/. Arguments are literal, with only
whole-token substitutions:
{goal}, {work}, {state}, {evidence}, and {expert}.
These expand to selected paths; {goal} is a goal-file path.
Goal bytes also arrive on stdin. Requires lists external command names.
There is no shell interpolation or permission field.
.PP
Run the entry through Record. Default host mode has ordinary host write, read,
and network authority. Separate directories, snapshots, and hash postchecks do
not prevent deliberate evidence alteration or change-and-restore races.
Automated source review supplies no security boundary.
.PP
Optional -entry-boundary cage runs the entry through Cage -net. Fixed grants
cover fresh work, state, child evidence, and private temporary storage.
Trait source, criteria, outer records, and snapshots are outside those grants.
Full networking and unrestricted host reads, including readable credentials,
remain available. A controller can bypass its children's normal Agent Cage;
only the optional outer Cage enforces its write boundary. Child records are
controller-writable in either mode, not independently trusted Trait evidence.
.PP
Entries receive TRAIT_AGENT, TRAIT_EXPERT, TRAIT_WORK, TRAIT_STATE,
TRAIT_EVIDENCE, TRAIT_GOAL, TRAIT_TURNS, and TRAIT_TIMEOUT.
A selected model is supplied as ASK_MODEL. Thin adapters preserve existing
team contracts; no provider client, model loop, or scheduler is added.
.SH OUTPUT
As stages complete, authoring produces expert/; eval emits no replacement.
Other outputs include the selected REQUEST.md, CAPABILITIES.md, REVIEW.md,
reusable evaluation/, checked cases/ID/work/ snapshots, result.json, and
EVALUATION.md. Candidate availability alone is not case acceptance.
The result identifies supplied/generated case origin and observed outcomes.
.PP
Stdout contains the same final JSON as result.json; progress goes to stderr.
Early failures may return only diagnostics. Private work, source, state,
proposals, streams, and model evidence remain under
.IR ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/trait/runs/RANDOM .
Retain referenced records. evaluated_sha256 identifies the selected definition.
Trait rechecks definition, source, and evaluation identities after execution
and checking; drift returns 125. Hashes identify bytes and modes, not quality.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Preserve child outcomes including 2 unfinished, 3 declined, 75 waiting,
125 uncertain/boundary failure, and 130 interrupted. Independent case rejection
and review rejection return 2; broken checks retain their status.
Invalid usage is 2, local failure 1, local subprocess timeout 124, and missing
commands 127. Hone's no-lesson outcome remains distinguishable.
Inspect the recorded phase; a number alone does not identify its meaning.
.SH DISTRIBUTION
The standalone core builds with Go 1.26+ and uses installed public commands.
From the repository root, scripts/build trait bundle creates independent
packages. With Go 1.26+ and Python 3.9+, scripts/package-trait --runtime PREFIX
--output FILE packages Trait and selected Bench programs through Bundle.
Select packages through .build/bin or --bin-dir. A bare executable lacks the
required package receipt and assets. The output executable must be new.
.PP
Recipients need no Go compiler or source checkout to launch Trait. Provider
access, credentials, Cage backend, and authored-capability dependencies remain
external; native authoring may require a compiler. Missing dependencies are
reported, never automatically installed. All actions may call configured
models. Offline fixtures prove process contracts, not real capability quality.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bundle (1),
.BR hire (1),
.BR agent (1),
.BR hone (1),
.BR brief (1),
.BR record (1),
.BR cage (1)

.SH EXPECTED REFUSAL
Case metadata may set expected_exit to 2 and outputs to an empty array.
Omission expects exit 0 and one or more regular-file outputs.
A separate check must verify the concrete refusal reason and no false completion;
status alone does not accept. Other expected statuses are invalid.
The check receives TRAIT_EXECUTION_EXIT, TRAIT_EXECUTION_STATUS (recorded JSON),
TRAIT_EXECUTION_STATE and TRAIT_EXECUTION_EVIDENCE.
Controller state and child records retain the selected boundary trust limits.
Unknown, interrupted and infrastructure outcomes cannot be expected successes.
